      "observed": "The schematic instructs “Short R13, R14 for Serial Servo,” but R13 is a 2.2 kΩ resistor in the MAX3485 bias network and R14 is a 0 Ω jumper in a PWM bus-pin mapping. The servo signal paths reach the shared serial node NET0031 through R8 and R21, both shown as 0 Ω jumpers; the instruction does not tell the assembler to close those paths.",
      "expected": "Serial mode should connect both servo signal pins to the shared MAX3485 bus by populating the appropriate 0 Ω links. The specification identifies R13 and R14 as those links, but in this drawing those references do not serve that role; the serial-mode instruction should identify the actual signal-path jumpers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
