          "quote": "Short R13, R14 for Serial Servo; R13 2.2k; R14 0; R8 0; R21 0. Sheet /, page 1."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Serial mode (populate R13/R14, per the explicit schematic annotation “Short R13, R14 for Serial Servo”): J3-pin3 and J8-pin3 are tied together into one shared bus node and driven by U1. Page 1."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Following the drawing's serial-mode instruction leaves the servo signal paths disconnected from the shared serial bus, so serial servos are unlikely to communicate. Shorting R13 as instructed would instead alter the MAX3485 bias network.",
      "confidence": 0.91
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The serial-servo assembly instruction names the wrong jumpers in this schematic. The actual servo-to-serial-bus links are R8 and R21, while R13 is a 2.2 kΩ bias resistor and R14 belongs to a PWM mapping path."
}

